  "comparison_limits": [
    "Three accepted cold boots after provisioning; first-boot filesystem growth and setup are excluded.",
    "These measurements qualify the combined fastboot and no-camera configuration. They do not isolate the contribution of asynchronous BPMP debugfs, quieter console output or disabled CSI camera probing.",
    "The retained custom minimal R39.2.1 UEFI/QSPI is shared with the bench baseline. These results do not qualify the full UEFI firmware generated by this repository.",
    "No camera or PCIe FFC endpoint was attached. C7 remains enabled at Gen2 in Linux; an attached FFC endpoint and camera-enabled operation are not qualified by these runs.",
    "The SCPI command-send reference includes command/output latency and board POR holdoff. The electrical power edge was not measured, and no approximately 2-second holdoff was subtracted.",
    "Quiet logging produced zero observable Linux-start banners in all three captures. Distinct qualification boot identifiers were checked privately, but the UART banner heuristic cannot exclude an unobservable intervening restart.",
    "CUDA readiness verifies a 65,536-element integer computation. It does not establish model loading, inference-server readiness or absence of earlier CUDA use by other services.",
    "The SSH milestone is an identification banner only. The UART milestone is a normal username prompt; neither measures successful authentication.",
    "UART receive timestamps and the 0.1-second SSH polling interval limit timing precision; no wire-byte or electrical-edge instrumentation was used."
